exports[`screens > doctor and init 1`] = `
"$ agentcurfew doctor <project>
[exit 1]
12 checks: 4 passed, 1 failed, 7 not applicable
  not applicable  agentcurfew.policy.json follows the schema [invalid-policy]
  passed          Every agent configuration file can be parsed [unparsable-config]
  passed          No file is named almost like one an agent reads [misnamed-file]
  passed          MCP files use the key their agents read [wrong-servers-key]
  not applicable  Remote servers in .mcp.json say their type [missing-mcp-type]
  passed          No project file silently overrides another [local-overrides-project]
  not applicable  No MCP server is defined twice in different ways [conflicting-mcp-server]
  failed          No deprecated file or setting is used [deprecated-format]
  not applicable  Every entry of the policy still matches something [stale-policy-entry]
  not applicable  The agentcurfew hook finds agentcurfew [agentcurfew-hook-missing]
  not applicable  A project with depcurfew.json has the depcurfew hook [depcurfew-hook-missing]
  not applicable  The depcurfew hook finds depcurfew [depcurfew-hook-broken]

WARNING  deprecated-format  .cursorrules
  Cursor calls .cursorrules deprecated; use rules in .cursor/rules/*.mdc
  fix: Move the content to the replacement named in the message.
  source: https://cursor.com/help/customization/rules

INFO  deprecated-format  .gemini/settings.json
  Gemini CLI calls httpUrl of the server old deprecated; use url with type http
  fix: Move the content to the replacement named in the message.
  source: https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/blob/3fd7d263466b9e5d30b2da1ebf85dae956a0fb86/packages/core/src/tools/mcp-client.ts

WARNING  deprecated-format  .gemini/settings.json
  Gemini CLI calls tools.exclude deprecated; use deny rules of the policy engine
  fix: Move the content to the replacement named in the message.
  source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/main/docs/reference/configuration.md

Failed: 2 problems at level warning or above (change with --fail-on or doctor.failOn).
"
`;

